Source: boswas-android
Section: otherosfs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Boswas OS Platform Team <os-platform@boswas.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), python3:any
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: boswas-android
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Boswas OS Android runtime manager (Waydroid) and APK installer
 Manages the optional Android runtime of Boswas OS and the Android apps in
 it. The runtime itself (Waydroid, from the Waydroid project's signed
 repository) is not part of this package: it is installed only when a user
 chooses to, through the boswas-sysops helper, and never starts on its own.
 .
  * boswas-android status / check: runtime, compatibility (binder, Wayland,
    processor, kernel, graphics, disk, Secure Boot), images, session,
    storage, network and the Google Play assessment; --json output
  * runtime install, init, update, repair, remove and service control,
    each authorised through pkexec and boswas-sysops
  * APK inspection (package, version, native ABIs, split APKs, signing
    certificates) before anything is installed; ARM-only and split APKs are
    refused with an explanation, and APKs are never modified or re-signed
  * install, launch and remove Android apps; F-Droid on request
 .
 Google Play is not available: Boswas OS has no Google Mobile Services
 licence and never downloads Google's apps.
